+## Optional additional audits
 
 From this directory, run `python3 verify_independent_census.py`. It regenerates the symmetry orbits and associativity equations, verifies the necessary linear-completion equations, compares the optimized census with a replay bypassing nonlinear shortcuts, and independently reconstructs the `Ad(SU(3)_4)` tensor from its Pieri graph. The results are 220 self-dual rings and 49 non-self-dual rings (47 with one dual pair and two with two dual pairs).
 
 The replay shares the existing fraction-free linear-completion routine and basis parametrization. It is an additional reproducibility check, not a wholly independent implementation or a formal verification. It does not read the stored witness records.
+
+Run `python3 verify_additional_audits.py` for the second revision round's targeted checks. It verifies the repaired quadratic cutoff by exact fractions, computes the relevant 864 cyclotomic moments and 19 joint trace vectors directly, compares all 14 induction/indicator cases with direct low-column enumeration, compares all 11 residual Gram cases with direct high-column enumeration, and certifies complete interval coverage and upper endpoints for the three quartic generator ranges.
+
+The latter audit shares the field data, certified root intervals, and construction of individual restriction-column sets. Its interval ranges are derived by Lagrange interpolation and divided differences, independently of the original fixed cutoffs and padding. It does not independently establish the categorical assumptions. Both optional commands passed; their current output is recorded in `../additional_verification_round2.txt`.
 
